    "tpa_score_new": null,
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": null,
    "course_pol_en": "Class Attendance:\nAttendance is an integral part of the course and is expcted from all students. If a student has a serious illness that results in missing class for more\nthan one week, documentation must be scanned and provided to the instructor via email and/or FCU apps.\n\nPolicy on Missed Exams and Coursework:\nAny work or exam submitted after the due date will be considered late and receive a grade of zero. \n\nThe instructor is solely responsible for determining whether provisions will be made for unforeseen circumstances. You must report these circumstances as soon as possible after the event. You may be required to provide evidences.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Academic misconduct refers to practices that a student or a researcher is aware of but deliberately and significantly deviates from the<br />\ngenreallyaccepted academic behavior, such as fabrication, falsification, plagiarism and any act of dishonesty in any forms.</div>\n\n<div>Academic&nbsp;&nbsp;misconduct can be divided into five types including</div>\n\n<div>1. inappropriate data&nbsp;collection or result obtention</div>\n\n<div>2. fabrication (falsification) of the assignment&nbsp;data</div>\n\n<div>3. plagiarism</div>\n\n<div>4. inappropriate authorship or designation&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>5. suplicate submission&nbsp;and application</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><u><strong>Penalties</strong></u> for academic misconduct can range from a grade of zero of the assignment(s)/assessment(s) to a penalty as severe as suspension formultiple dishonest acts reported.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": null
  },
